course: dictionary
lesson: 5781
title: A red word in the tomato
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you cannot see, like lycopene. Read the words around it to find out what it is. «As a tomato ripens its green fades and a red pigment called lycopene builds up.» The word «called» is a clue: the word after it is the name, and «pigment» tells you it is a colouring.
explain: Lycopene is the red colour in some foods. «Scientists call a tomato a fruit because it holds seeds, it turns red as it ripens by making a red colour called lycopene.» So lycopene is what makes the red colour, not the red colour itself.
explain: Some words describe what a substance does, not what it looks like. Lycopene is an antioxidant, which means it may help protect the body's cells. The word "may" matters: it says this is what scientists think, not something that is always proven.
fact: Lycopene is a natural red colouring found in tomatoes, watermelon and pink grapefruit.
fact: An antioxidant is a substance that may help protect the body's cells.
fact: Lycopene is a noun, because it is the name of a substance.
fact: «Tomatoes ripen faster next to bananas because bananas give off a gas called ethylene.» Ethylene is a gas, not a colouring.
fact: Tomatoes first came from South America.
exercise: «As a tomato ripens its green fades and a red pigment called lycopene builds up.» What is lycopene? | *A red colouring | A gas given off by bananas | A seed inside a fruit | A green leaf
exercise: Which food is NOT named as a home of lycopene? | *Bananas | Pink grapefruit | Tomatoes | Watermelon
exercise: Lycopene is an antioxidant. What may it help to do? | Turn the fruit green | Make the fruit taste sour | Make bananas ripen faster | *Protect the body's cells
test: «Tomatoes ripen faster next to bananas because bananas give off a gas called ethylene.» What is ethylene? | A kind of seed | A red colouring | *A gas given off by bananas | A pink grapefruit
test: In «a red pigment called lycopene», what does the word «called» tell you? | It shows the sentence is a question | It means the pigment is green | *The word after it is the name of the pigment | It means the pigment is a fruit
exam: Which best explains what lycopene is? | A gas given off by bananas | *A natural red colouring in some foods that may help protect the body's cells | A green fruit | A seed that holds a tomato together
